      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A new cell electrochemical detecting system has been constructed based on the hyposmotic principle, in which the electrochemical signals have been strengthened by about 109.75% for the signal at about +0.70 V and 532.94% for the signal at about +1.03 V. The electrochemical detection limits of the cells have been improved by one order of magnitude. The individual concentrations of intracellular purines have been obtained."},
